# Template only. Copy to frontend/.env.local and fill in.
#
# Save as plain UTF-8 with NO byte-order mark. A BOM becomes part of the first
# key name, so Vite parses `<BOM>VITE_API_URL` and `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`
# reads `undefined` — the app then renders but every API call goes to the Vite
# dev server instead of the API. On Windows, PowerShell's `>` and `Set-Content`
# both write a BOM by default; use `-Encoding utf8NoBOM`, or write the file from
# an editor set to "UTF-8" rather than "UTF-8 with BOM".
#
# Only variables prefixed `VITE_` are exposed to the browser. Never put a secret
# here — anything in this file ships inside the client bundle.

# Origin + base path of the API. Must include /api/v1.
# Required: src/lib/apiClient.ts throws at import if it is missing.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
